Initial sketch to see if TMS7000 is doable

The experimental board set up has

0000-00FF	Onboard registers (00-7F only)
0100-01FF	I/O. Onboard and external (CF is at 0x90)
0200-04FF	Used for loading then replaced with udata/stacks
0500-3FFF	Common space (actually bankable 0200-3FFF)
4000-FFFF	Banked space

The wiring is a 4bit x 2 mux as with the 8085 but it's fed from port A.
Port A starts at 0xFF but this doesn't matter much as our ROM can configure
it anyway. This does mean a 70x1 part will not work.

The low 16K and the upper 48K each use a nybble of port A

ROM enable maps the ROM over stuff and is driven by the OUT1 pin on the
16x50A.

It's not a useful setup. It'll start and go through some early boot up but
it's too slow to run Fuzix.
